				"actualAnswer": "=Inputs: Topic: {{ $('Set Input').item.json.Topic }}\\nDescription: {{ $('Set Input').item.json.Desciption }}",
				"prompt": "You are an expert evaluator for photorealistic text-to-image prompts tailored to Indian healthcare hiring articles.\n\nTask: Given topic + description and the image prompt output by the agent, evaluate whether the prompt meets the agent's system requirements and is ready for use with text-to-image models.\n\nScoring goals (1–5). Check and report evidence for each:\n1. **Format** — Single continuous paragraph with no headings or extra text. Verify character length ≤ 1024.\n2. **Style** — Photorealistic, highly detailed, editorial-quality language suitable for professional article illustration.\n3. **Domain specificity** — Clearly references Indian healthcare hiring context: Indian medical environments, diverse healthcare professionals, recruitment cues (interviews, job fair, onboarding, digital hiring) or visible hiring elements.\n4. **Visual detail** — Includes attire, background elements, lighting/composition, realistic props (medical equipment, banners) and professional expressions.\n5. **Restrictions** — No text overlays, logos, or unrealistic/fictional elements.\n6. **Model-readiness** — Prompt is concise, descriptive, and optimized for text-to-image models (no API instructions, no bracketed metadata).\n7. **Creativity & fidelity** — Evokes a compelling, specific image that supports the article’s intent.\n\nOutput required. Return ONLY this JSON:\n{\n  \"extended_reasoning\": \"<step-by-step evidence mapped to each of the 7 checks above; include quoted short excerpts from {actual_answer} to justify each check>\",\n  \"reasoning_summary\": \"<one-sentence overall verdict>\",\n  \"score\": <integer 1-5>,\n  \"char_count\": <integer character length of generated prompt>\n}\n\nScoring rubric:\n5 = Meets all checks; single-paragraph, ≤1024 chars, domain-specific, highly detailed, no forbidden elements, model-ready.\n4 = Minor issue (e.g., slightly generic phrasing or small missing detail) but otherwise usable.\n3 = Several issues (e.g., weak domain signals, partial format problems, or missing realism).\n2 = Significant problems (e.g., off-niche, includes disallowed elements, or poor structure).\n1 = Fails to meet major requirements (multi-paragraph, >1024 chars, off-topic, or contains logos/text).\n\nNotes:\n- Treat the inputs as the editorial brief for relevance checks and quote it only in analysis if needed.\n- In `extended_reasoning` be concise. For each check include a one-line verdict and 1–2 short quoted examples from the generated prompt.\n- Return nothing else.\n",
				"options": {
					"inputPrompt": "{actual_answer}\n\n{expected_answer}"
				}
			},
